<title>MEXICO: Mexico sets quota for tariff-free dry milk imports.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets quota for tariff-free dry milk imports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Trade Ministry on Wednesday set the national quota for tariff-free powdered milk imports into Mexico at 120,000 tonnes for 1997.</p>
<p>The ministry said via the government's Official Gazette that the quota applies to member nations of the World Trade Organization.</p>
<p>It said 80,000 tonnes of the total duty-free allocation went to the United States under a favored-nation status under the North American Free Trade Agreement.</p>
<p>The quota applied to powdered milk with at least 1.5 percent fat content and without colorings or sweeteners, the ministry added. No quota was given for powdered milk with a fat content below 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
